; A fixed BOOL or NULL value carried by a CHOICE ARM. bool and null are single-byte CBOR specials
; with no encoding variation, so under `--preserve-encodings` they contribute NO binding target at
; all: the value itself is fixed (nothing to store) and it has no encoding sidecar either (unlike a
; fixed uint/nint, which carries an `Sz`, or a fixed text, which carries a `StringEncoding`). The
; arm's deserialize must therefore VERIFY the constant without binding it — a `let {} = ` LHS over
; an empty binding list emits `let  = ();`, which rustfmt rejects and the run dies at exit 1 with
; ZERO files written. The member-position path has always guarded this (records.rs
; `generate_array_struct_deserialization`); this fixture pins the CHOICE-ARM half, which reaches
; the guard through two separate enum-side sites:
;   map_bool_arm / map_null_arm — a collapsed map-rep arm with a fixed key, whose value read is
;                     emitted by `make_keyed_map_variant_deser_code`. The `{var}_key_encoding` is
;                     bound separately by the key read, so it does NOT make the VALUE's binding
;                     list non-empty; only the value's own sidecar would, and a special has none.
;   arr_bool_arm / arr_null_arm — an array-rep group-choice arm, emitted by the generic
;                     `EnumVariantData::RustType` deser path. Under preserve the variant still
;                     carries `len_encoding`, so the constructor stays the struct-variant spelling.
;   type_choice_bool — a bare TYPE choice (`rep = None`) through the same generic path, where the
;                     variant is genuinely field-less under every profile and the constructor is
;                     the `Ok(T::True)` name-it-don't-call-it spelling.
; The preserve profile is load-bearing for all five: under the default profile a fixed-value arm
; takes the verify-only exemption unconditionally, so the empty-binding case never arises. Under
; preserve the verify-only arm still needs the terminating `;`, because the `Fixed` deserialize
; branch emits a trailing `()` value EXPRESSION there (the default branch emits no value at all).
;
; NOT spelled here, deliberately:
;   `t = null / tstr` — a two-arm type choice with `null` never becomes a fixed-value arm at all;
;     it lowers to `Option<String>`, so it exercises nothing of this class.
;   `t = true / null / tstr` — a THREE-arm type choice whose bool and null arms share the CBOR
;     Special type routes through the brute-force try-each-arm dispatch, which still emits an
;     unterminated `()` before its appended `Ok(())` (a distinct site from the two above, and
;     equally broken before and after this fixture's fix). Adding it here would make the whole
;     fixture ungeneratable; it belongs with whatever pins that site.
; Fixed specials in ordinary MEMBER position (not arm position) live in `fixed_bool_member.cddl`;
; the general map-rep group-choice dispatch/key-verification coverage lives in
; `group_choice_map.cddl`.
map_bool_arm = { flag: true // label: tstr }
map_null_arm = { absent: null // label: tstr }
arr_bool_arm = [ flag: true // label: tstr ]
arr_null_arm = [ absent: null // label: tstr ]
type_choice_bool = true / tstr
